{
  "_comment": "DEV DECK - Sworn Wild (Paladin / Druid), 50 hand-authored dev cards (owner-designed, 2026-08-19). NON-CANON: every card carries dev:true so shipped-pool queries can exclude them. Phase 1 = AUTHOR + FLAG: cards whose behavior has a live engine path carry structured effects; every behavior the engine cannot yet honor carries an effectsFlag starting 'DEV NOT-IMPLEMENTED' (visible machinery debt; the validator reports it and does not fail). That flag list IS the arc plan for the implementation sessions that follow. Type lines carry the Beast modifier per the 2026-08-18 ruling (Beast = non-magical non-sapient animal, printed never derived, ordered Modifier-Organism-Role); Angels are sapient and are NOT Beasts. Armor carriers print the FULL inverted companion clause (2026-08-18 inversion) with X substituted. Vocal subtypes corrected 2026-08-19 (owner ruling): Druid Vocal Constructs are RITE, Paladin's are BLESSING. 'Performance' was retired entirely and the borrowed Utterance (a Doom-Whisperer subtype) was wrong for the same reason. ARC A (2026-08-19): the destroy primitive landed — the seven destroy cards are LIVE. Destroy is a DIFFERENT EVENT from sacrifice (owner ruling): it never fires on-sacrifice listeners, while generic leave/death triggers fire for both, and the card lands in its OWNER's Dead Zone either way. ARC B (2026-08-20): Beast-subtype reach landed — subtype targeting, group scopes, the Dead Zone filter and the `ready` op. Subtype tokens are AUTHORED in this file and read through catalog lookups; they are deliberately NOT carried on the runtime Card, because Card objects serialize into recordings.",
